# Git: no push by the agent

The user performs **all** `git push` operations personally.

- **Never** run `git push`, `git push -u`, or any remote-updating push variant.
- Do not offer to push unless the user explicitly asks — and even then, remind them that pushes are theirs only, unless they clearly override this rule in that message.
- Commits are still only when the user asks (existing project convention).
- After commits, stop at local commit and leave push to the user.
